CSS styling
1 inline styling is done using style attribute
used to style individual element
it has higest priority

2 internal styling applied using style tag which is defined within the head section
we go for it when we hace multiple blocks requiring styling for diff elements
individual single document having a lot of elements to style
drawback limited only to one individual document

3 external styling is applied using link tag in the head section
external css file is created with .css extension and linked to the html document
we can use it across multiple documents using the link tag which is written in the head section of the html document
it is the most efficient way to style multiple documents with the same css file

we can use all 3 stylings in a single html document but the priority is inline > internal > external
how to reesolve conflict between internal and external styling
if there is a conflict between internal and external styling then the internal styling will take precedence over the external styling because it has higher priority

IF :
in internal styling color is given as blue
in external styling color is orange 
internal is applied first then external is applied and it will override the internal styling and the 
final color will be orange because it is the latest applied styling

